---
// SectionProblem.astro - 01 / THE PROBLEM
---

<section id="the-problem" class="py-20 border-b border-tide-border bg-tide-bg relative scroll-mt-14">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    
    <!-- Section label -->
    <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-tide-accent font-mono mb-4">
      01 / THE PROBLEM
    </div>

    <!-- 2-Column Split -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-12 items-start">
      
      <!-- Left Column: Headline & Technical Narrative -->
      <div class="lg:col-span-5 space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-tide-text leading-tight font-mono">
          Unorchestrated agents create silent state corruption.
        </h2>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-tide-text-secondary leading-relaxed font-sans">
          Running autonomous coding agents inside raw terminal tabs leads to concurrent Git index collisions, orphaned background processes, and frozen terminal event loops.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Right Column: 3 Numbered Problem Blocks with Dividers -->
      <div class="lg:col-span-7 divide-y divide-tide-border">
        
        <!-- Problem 01 -->
        <div class="py-6 first:pt-0 space-y-2">
          <div class="flex items-baseline gap-3">
            <span class="text-xs font-mono font-bold text-tide-accent">01</span>
            <h3 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-tide-text font-mono">
              Working tree race conditions & index deadlocks
            </h3>
          </div>
          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-tide-text-secondary leading-relaxed pl-7 font-sans">
            When multiple agents modify the working tree concurrently, they overwrite uncommitted changes, deadlock on <code class="text-tide-danger font-mono">.git/index.lock</code>, and produce contaminated branches that require manual rebase surgery.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Problem 02 -->
        <div class="py-6 space-y-2">
          <div class="flex items-baseline gap-3">
            <span class="text-xs font-mono font-bold text-tide-accent">02</span>
            <h3 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-tide-text font-mono">
              Orphaned NT process trees and port exhaustion
            </h3>
          </div>
          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-tide-text-secondary leading-relaxed pl-7 font-sans">
            Subprocesses spawned by agent tool calls—compilers, watchers, dev servers—frequently survive shell exits. Windows process hierarchies leak zombie processes that hold network ports like <code class="text-tide-text font-mono">localhost:3000</code> and drain host RAM.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Problem 03 -->
        <div class="py-6 last:pb-0 space-y-2">
          <div class="flex items-baseline gap-3">
            <span class="text-xs font-mono font-bold text-tide-accent">03</span>
            <h3 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-tide-text font-mono">
              VT100 burst floods and UI thread starvation
            </h3>
          </div>
          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-tide-text-secondary leading-relaxed pl-7 font-sans">
            Unbounded compiler diagnostics and high-throughput LLM streaming saturate stdout pipes. Without frame-paced PTY consumption, terminal emulators lock their rendering thread and drop user keyboard events.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>

  </div>
</section>
